    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d208">

                <pb facs="0344" n="244" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg244"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.00/3371</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The German Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bülow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American
                        Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>)<anchor n="36"
                        xml:id="d208-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-08">August 8, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I have the honor to inform Your
                    Excellency that, on the basis of the law in regard to the Chief of State of the
                    German Reich of August 1, 1934, which entered into force on August 2, 1934, the
                    office of President of the Reich has been united with that of the Reich
                    Chancellor. As a result of this, the powers which have hitherto pertained to the
                    President of the Reich have passed to the Leader and Reich Chancellor Adolf
                    Hitler.</p>
                <p>The official designation of the German Chief of State is “the Leader and Reich
                    Chancellor” for internal German official communications, and “the German Reich
                    Chancellor” in official communications with foreign countries.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bülow</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d208-f1" n="36" type="source" xml:id="d208-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted to the Department by the Ambassador in his despatch No. 1146, August
                    13; received August 24.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
